ions.\n- 2026-10-05: Ring producer delivered contact/clearance/speed edits. Parent FIX-FIRST: 0.11rad/s forms a full axial band after only12.6deg contact sweep; coverage must be physically sufficient or represented as explicitly compressed high-speed work. Correction requested; lifecycle8turn endpoint test must not simply be weakened.\n- 2026-10-05: All four follow-up Sonnet requests exhausted HTTP429 retries. Their partial files are preserved. Fresh inherited OpenAI workers now own shell, ring correction, mechanical classification and camera/tool compatibility. Previous failed seats closed. Different-provider review remains mandatory and is not inferred from unavailable reviewers.\n- 2026-10-05 (resume): Pasteur, Lorentz, Aristotle, Gibbs, Leibniz and Nash all ended with HTTP429 retry exhaustion. Partial files preserved. Parent (now claude-opus-5-5) takes over Leibniz's integration ownership. Producer routing moves to `codex exec -m zai/glm-5.3` (unique proxy conversations); parent Anthropic review plus GLM read-only reviews provide provider diversity against OpenAI producers.\n- 2026-10-05: Full suite found renderLease light-restore defect: lights were recorded twice (light record, then hidden map after being hidden), so restore re-hid every scene light. Parent fix: early return after light record (renderLease.ts visit). renderLease tests 6/6.\n- 2026-10-05: Housing 3.687 mm finding resolved as classification artifact (mechanical-review/housing-resolution.md): single 2-of-3 parity sample at r 6.01 mm inside a 19.27 mm housing bore, zero triangle crossings, open-shell housing.\n- 2026-10-05: GLM ring sampler review SHIP (ring/independent-review-glm.md); integration/browser not certified by it. Existing verify-ring-inspection.mjs 7/7 cases PASS on integrated lifecycle at :5199 (runtime/ring-integrated-1/report.json).\n- 2026-10-05: Dispatched GLM producers: clearance v3 (camera/clearance-v3-spec.md) and lifecycle verifier (runtime/lifecycle-verifier-spec.md); GLM re